---
// /control-rig/ — the FS Control Rig product page.
//
// IT IS TWO WORDS (Adrian, 2026-09-03: "It's called Control Rig not ControlRig btw").
// Everywhere a reader can see it. The exceptions are not names of ours and do not move:
// ControlRigDynamics is Epic's own plugin, `controlrig.plugin` is the licence capability
// key, and /control-rig/ is the URL.
//
// NEW 2026-09-03 on Adrian's instruction ("Start a new page called Control Rig"), the third
// of the three product pages the 2026-08-31 naming ruling calls for: Armature, Pipeline,
// Control Rig (StandingOrders/Knowledge/product-state.md, Naming).
//
// THREE CARDS, EACH WITH ITS OWN VIDEO (Adrian, 2026-09-03). His card titles and his one
// line under each, verbatim; card 1's title is his correction the same day, "Procedurally
// built" over "Procedural Control Rigs". All three clips are in as of that afternoon — he
// shot 2 and 3 himself. The unfinished-plate branch below stays anyway: a fourth card, or a
// clip pulled for a re-shoot, must hold the row's shape rather than collapse it.
//
// CARD 1 IS THE PAGE'S OLD TOP VIDEO, PING-PONGED (his ask). proof-controlrig-pingpong.mp4
// is the 7.007s original followed by its own reverse with the duplicate seam frame dropped,
// so it runs 13.972s and loops with no jump at either end. Built with ffmpeg from
// proof-controlrig.mp4, which stays in place because the homepage still uses it.
//
// EVERY VIDEO AUTOPLAYS (his ask), through the site's own LazyVideos component: muted,
// looping, inline, nothing downloads or plays until it nears the viewport, and
// prefers-reduced-motion gets the poster still and no motion at all. That component is the
// one place a playback fix lands, so this page must not hand-roll its own player.
//
// NO DOWNLOAD DOOR YET. The 1.0.5 artifact is cut but the account page's download row is
// held until the site pass is done (Website lane, Web/2026-09-03_controlrig-download-row/
// PREPARED.md). When it goes live, the door is the account page, not a public link.
//
// No Control Rig docs exist on the site, so there is no "Read the docs" door either. The
// tiers on /tools/ are the one door this page has.
//
// "PREFLIGHT" IS AN ILLEGAL TERM (Adrian, 2026-09-03: "Preflight is an illegal term to use
// in Fabricator Studio. It's called Pre build"). The check step is PRE BUILD on every
// customer-facing surface. Do not reintroduce it from the plugin's README or its Python,
// which still carry the old word internally.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NavBar from '../../components/NavBar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Masthead from '../../components/Masthead.astro';
import BracketButton from '../../components/BracketButton.astro';
import LazyVideos from '../../components/LazyVideos.astro';

const TITLE = 'Control Rig | FabricatorStudio';
const DESCRIPTION =
  'FS Control Rig for Unreal Engine 5.8. An Animator-Friendly Modular Control Rig, built in one click from the same export that rigs your character in Maya.';

// Adrian's three cards. Title and line are HIS WORDS, verbatim; nothing here is a rewrite.
// Rewritten by him 2026-09-03 in the afternoon, replacing his own morning one-liners. ONE
// character was changed and he was told: he typed "Prodecurally Built." and the word is
// Procedurally, which he had ruled himself hours earlier. Everything else stands exactly as
// he wrote it, punctuation and all, including the trailing full stops on the titles.
// A card carries EITHER a clip or a still, and `video: null, image: null` renders the
// unfinished plate. Cards 2 and 3 are the Captain's own captures, supplied 2026-09-03 from
// D:/Videos/FabricatorStudio/ControlRig/ (Prebuild.mov, Dynamics.mov) and encoded for the
// web: audio stripped, since an autoplaying video is always muted, which also took Prebuild
// from 13.6 MB to 1.1 MB and Dynamics from 28.4 MB to 2.7 MB with no change to the picture.
// NEITHER IS PING-PONGED, unlike card 1: card 2 runs a check list through to a finished rig,
// and backwards it would show the checks un-checking themselves. Each poster is that clip's
// own last frame, so a card shows its payoff before it plays and to anyone on reduced
// motion.
const CARDS = [
  {
    title: 'Procedurally Built.',
    accent: 'cobalt',
    line: 'All FS exports now carry rig build data, application agnostic. Build FabricatorStudio Modular rigs, procedurally and automatically when using Armature to build your skeleton, both in Maya and Unreal.',
    video: '/proof/proof-controlrig-pingpong.mp4',
    poster: '/proof/proof-controlrig.jpg',
    image: null,
    alt: 'The same character and control rig shown in Maya and then in Unreal.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Quick and Friendly.',
    accent: 'plasma',
    line: 'Pre build inspection checks before it builds and will help you fix your skeleton. Animator-Friendly Rigs built by a AAA veteran.',
    video: '/proof/controlrig-prebuild.mp4',
    poster: '/proof/controlrig-prebuild.jpg',
    image: null,
    alt: 'The FS Control Rig builder checking a character, then the built rig in the Unreal Control Rig editor.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Auto Dynamics.',
    accent: 'ember',
    line: 'Using the Dynamic Chain in Armature will automatically apply dynamic physics on your chain, with fully customizable presets.',
    video: '/proof/controlrig-dynamics.mp4',
    poster: '/proof/controlrig-dynamics.jpg',
    image: null,
    alt: 'A cape simulating on the Archangel character in the Unreal Control Rig editor.',
  },
];
---
<BaseLayout title={TITLE} description={DESCRIPTION}>
  <NavBar />

  {/* THE SHARED MASTHEAD (Adrian, 2026-09-04): the wordmark, the underlined title, and the
      serif promise, same as Pricing, Maya Pipeline, Services and My Account.
      HIS TITLE AND HIS SUB, and the sub is SHORTER than what stood here: ", built in one
      click from the same export that rigs your character in Maya. No manual rigging." is
      cut. He gave the line; it is not a truncation of mine. */}
  <section id="cr-intro">
    <Masthead title="Unreal Control Rig" promise="An Animator-Friendly Modular Control Rig in Unreal Engine 5.8" />
    <div class="cr-ctas">
      <BracketButton kind="hard" href="/pricing/" label="See the plans" event="controlrig-plans" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="cr-cards">
    <div class="cr-grid">
      {CARDS.map((c) => (
        <article class="cr-card">
          <h3 class={'cr-card__title cr-card__title--' + c.accent}>{c.title}</h3>
          <div class="cr-card__media">
            {c.video ? (
              <video
                class="cr-card__video"
                data-lazyvid
                src={c.video}
                poster={c.poster}
                muted
                loop
                playsinline
                preload="none"
                aria-label={c.alt}
              ></video>
            ) : c.image ? (
              <img class="cr-card__still" src={c.image} alt={c.alt} loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1145" height="728" />
            ) : (
              /* Visibly unfinished, never a silent gap: the card holds its shape and says
                 what belongs here, so a missing clip reads as pending rather than broken. */
              <div class="cr-card__plate" aria-hidden="true"><span>CLIP PENDING</span></div>
            )}
          </div>
          <p class="cr-card__line">{c.line}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="cr-facts">
    <dl class="cr-facts">
      {/* ENGINE AND READS REMOVED 2026-09-04 on his instruction. What went: "Unreal Engine
          5.8. Dynamic chains need the engine's ControlRigDynamics plugin enabled." and "An
          Armature 2.1.8 or newer export, or the Studio Pipeline's Maya exporter. Older
          exports are refused by name and asked to re-export."
          The engine version still reaches a buyer: it is in the promise line at the top of
          this page and in the download row's own note on the account page. The Armature
          minimum now appears nowhere on the site, which is raised with him. */}
      <div class="cr-fact">
        <dt>Included in</dt>
        {/* HIS LINE. He wrote "Freelance Animation", which is not one of the tier names;
            the two bands carrying controlrig.plugin are Freelance Animator and Freelance
            Tech Art + Animation. Placed as written and raised with him rather than
            silently corrected, because the words on a price surface are his. */}
        <dd>Freelance Animation, Pro and Enterprise. Not in base Freelance Tech Art.</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <Footer />
  {/* After the videos, per the component's own contract. */}
  <LazyVideos />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .cr-ctas { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.75rem; }

  .cr-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .cr-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .cr-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.9rem; }
  /* The frame owns the aspect, so all three cards line up whether their clip has landed
     yet or not. 4:3 matches the clip we have. */
  .cr-card__media {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    border-radius: 18px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--carbon);
    border: 1px solid var(--iron-2);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }
  .cr-card__video { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  /* CONTAIN, not cover: this one is a screenshot of a window, and cropping it to fill a
     4:3 frame would cut the checks off the side. It sits on the frame's own ground. */
  .cr-card__still { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; }
  .cr-card__plate {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, var(--carbon) 0 12px, var(--iron) 12px 24px);
  }
  .cr-card__plate span {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    color: var(--bone-faint);
  }
  /* ONE ACCENT PER CARD (Adrian, 2026-09-03: "give each title of the cards a distinct
     color"). Each is the token whose own stated meaning fits the card: COBALT is the
     structural accent, the skeleton and the rig data this card is about; PLASMA is the
     functional green the passing checks are already drawn in; EMBER carries the dynamics.
     One line each to swap if he wants them ordered differently. */
  .cr-card__title { margin: 0; font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.3; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .cr-card__title--cobalt { color: var(--cobalt); }
  .cr-card__title--plasma { color: var(--plasma); }
  .cr-card__title--ember  { color: var(--ember); }
  /* Bone, not bone-dim: his call, and it makes the card copy read as body text rather than
     as a caption under a picture. */
  .cr-card__line { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--bone); text-wrap: pretty; }

  .cr-facts { margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .cr-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .cr-fact { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .cr-fact dt { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.8125rem; letter-spacing: 0.3em; color: var(--bone); }
  .cr-fact dd { margin: 0; font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--bone-dim); text-wrap: pretty; }
</style>
